Appendix C: Proofs from Section 3 (Formal Problem Definition)

C.1 Governance Capacity Gap

Recall the definition:

GCG_t = 1 - \frac{H_t}{H_{\text{req}}(C_t)}.

Lemma C.1 (Normalization of GCG).
If H_{\text{req}}(C_t) > 0, then GCG_t \le 1, with GCG_t = 1 iff H_t = 0.

Proof. Since H_t \ge 0 and H_{\text{req}}(C_t) > 0, we have H_t / H_{\text{req}}(C_t) \ge 0, so GCG_t \le 1. Equality holds iff H_t / H_{\text{req}}(C_t) = 0, i.e., H_t = 0. \square

Lemma C.2 (GCG interpretation).
GCG_t > 0 iff H_t < H_{\text{req}}(C_t). GCG_t \le 0 iff H_t \ge H_{\text{req}}(C_t).

Proof. GCG_t > 0 \iff 1 - H_t/H_{\text{req}} > 0 \iff H_t/H_{\text{req}} < 1 \iff H_t < H_{\text{req}}. Similarly for the other direction. \square

