Appendix N: Simulation Parameters and Functional Forms

For the simulation protocol described in Section 13 of the main text, we specify concrete functional forms and parameter ranges.

N.1 Capability Evolution

\Delta C(a_t) = 
\begin{cases}
0.01 & \text{if } a_t = \text{slow} \\
0.05 & \text{if } a_t = \text{maintain} \\
0.10 & \text{if } a_t = \text{accelerate}
\end{cases}

N.2 Assurance Evolution

\Delta A(a_t) = 
\begin{cases}
+0.02 & \text{if } a_t = \text{slow} \\
+0.01 & \text{if } a_t = \text{maintain} \\
-0.01 & \text{if } a_t = \text{accelerate}
\end{cases}

(Acceleration reduces assurance because less time is spent on evaluation.)

N.3 Uncertainty Dynamics

U_{t+1} = \min\{1, U_t + 0.1 \Delta C(a_t) - 0.05 \Delta A(a_t)\}.

N.4 Residual Risk

R_{t+1} = \min\{1, R_t + 0.2 \Delta C(a_t) + 0.1 I_t - 0.1 \Delta A(a_t)\}.

N.5 Catastrophe Probability

P(\text{catastrophe}) = 1 - \exp\left(-\frac{R_t^2}{1 - U_t + \epsilon} - \frac{I_t^2}{G_t + \epsilon}\right),

where \epsilon = 10^{-6} is a small constant to avoid division by zero.

N.6 Threshold Function

\theta(T) = \min\{1, 0.5 + 0.3 I(T) + 0.2 R(T) + 0.1 \Delta C(T)\}.

N.7 Hard Constraint Parameters

R_{\max} = 0.8, \quad U_{\max} = 0.9, \quad H_{\min} = 0.3, \quad A_{\min}(T) = 0.2 + 0.3 I(T), \quad G_{\min}(T) = 0.2 + 0.3 I(T).

