   0.0 ┤──────────────────────────────────► Risk R
       0.0                           1.0
        (Inside the region: S(T) ≥ θ(T) and hard constraints hold)
```

Contraction Theorem (Theorem 1): If T_2 is riskier than T_1 (higher I, R, U, or ΔC) and both have same A, G, then T_2 ∈ 𝒜 ⇒ T_1 ∈ 𝒜.

```
