Z.7 Proof Sketch of Theorem 1 (Authorization Set Contraction)

```
Given:  I(T2) ≥ I(T1), R(T2) ≥ R(T1), U(T2) ≥ U(T1), ΔC(T2) ≥ ΔC(T1)
        A(T2) = A(T1), G(T2) = G(T1)

   S(T2) = A·G·(1−U2)·(1−R2)   ≤   A·G·(1−U1)·(1−R1) = S(T1)

   θ(T2) = min{1, θ0 + β_I·I2 + β_R·R2 + β_C·ΔC2}
         ≥ min{1, θ0 + β_I·I1 + β_R·R1 + β_C·ΔC1} = θ(T1)

Therefore:
   S(T2) ≥ θ(T2)  ⇒  S(T1) ≥ S(T2) ≥ θ(T2) ≥ θ(T1)

So T2 authorized ⇒ T1 authorized.
```

Diagram of the implication chain:

```
   S(T2) ≥ θ(T2)
        │
        ▼
   S(T1) ≥ S(T2)   (since S(T2) ≤ S(T1))
        │
        ▼
   S(T1) ≥ θ(T2)   (transitivity)
        │
        ▼
   S(T1) ≥ θ(T1)   (since θ(T2) ≥ θ(T1))
        │
        ▼
   T1 is authorized
```

