Z.8 Game‑Theoretic Payoff Matrix

Two laboratories, actions: slow (s) or accelerate (a).

```
                   Lab 2: slow              Lab 2: accelerate
   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │ Lab 1: slow    │   B                   │   B − b_rel        │
   ├────────────────┼───────────────────────┼────────────────────┤
   │ Lab 1: accel.  │   B + b_rel + b_abs − c │ B + b_abs − c − r │
   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Definitions:

```
   B     = baseline utility from mutual slowness (normalized)
   b_rel = relative advantage from being the only accelerator
   b_abs = absolute capability gain from accelerating
   c     = extra safety cost of accelerating
   r     = interaction risk cost when both accelerate
```

Prisoner’s dilemma conditions:

```
   Dominance:  b_rel + b_abs > c + r     (accelerate is best regardless)
   Inefficiency: b_abs < c + r           (mutual accel worse than mutual slow)
```

Payoff ordering: u_as > u_ss > u_aa > u_sa

