Z.9 Gate‑Induced Equilibrium Shift

Adding a binding gate changes the payoffs for accelerating by subtracting a denial cost κ·P(denial|a,A).

```
   Without Gate                        With Gate

   Lab2: slow   Lab2: accel           Lab2: slow        Lab2: accel
   ┌─────────────────────┐            ┌──────────────────────────┐
   │ B      | B−b_rel     │            │ B          | B−b_rel      │
   │────────┼────────────│            │────────────┼─────────────│
   │ B+b_rel+b_abs−c     │            │ B+b_rel+b_abs−c−κP  │ B+b_abs−c−r−κP │
   │        | B+b_abs−c−r │            │            |              │
   └─────────────────────┘            └──────────────────────────┘
```

For sufficiently large κ, acceleration is no longer dominant ⇒ (slow, slow) becomes unique Nash equilibrium.

